231
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:15,760
of Christ and rebirth. In 1885,

232
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:19,220
Carl Fabergé, the most famous court jeweler in history,

233
00:13:19,221 --> 00:13:22,020
began making a special series of annual Easter eggs

234
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:25,960
for his patron, Tsar Alexander III of Russia.

235
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:28,760
Inside each egg was a small surprise.

236
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:31,760
Each year, the mechanisms or surprises

237
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:34,460
became more complicated. That was what people looked

238
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:37,880
