239
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:39,980
Some of the more unique surprises

240
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,880
were what are called automatons.

241
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:44,320
They're small mechanical objects that, when wound up,

242
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:48,020
would move, walk, et cetera.

243
00:13:48,021 --> 00:13:50,020
When Nicholas II inherited the throne

244
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,660
after his father's death in 1894,

245
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:56,960
he expanded the tradition by ordering two eggs for each Easter.

246
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:59,160
Every egg was impossibly intricate

247
00:13:59,260 --> 00:14:03,060
and took more than 18 months to create and build.

248
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:06,700
In all, 50 imperial eggs were completed before the fall

249
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:09,040
of the Tsar in 1917.

250
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:12,140
Fabergé had the unique ability to bring together craftsmen

251
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:15,740
from different disciplines and to have them work cohesively

252
00:14:15,741 --> 00:14:17,540
together to create these eggs.

253
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:21,480
So they involved engravers, stone setters, stone cutters,

254
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:24,780
enamelists, goldsmiths, silversmiths, et cetera,

255
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:29,880
all working as one unit to create these works of art.

